# Erdős Problem #99 — Target A basis-pair shield contraction

**Date:** 2026-09-04  
**Branch:** `research/target-c-c97-caterpillar-fan-capacity-2026-09-04`  
**Run type:** exact strengthening of Section 174.5  
**Target:** locked three-channel Schur sector branch  
**Status:** LEVEL I STILL OPEN

## 1. Error of scale in the crude shield charge

Section 174.5 bounds the number of vertex-disjoint Schur paths meeting a basis-closed shield `W=widehat W_Sigma` by `|W|`. This is safe but not sharp for the Section 113 directed gammoid.

Fix the basis matching

`mu_0:B->Z`.

The directed graph has

- unmatched conflict edges oriented left-to-right;
- matching edges `z->mu_0^{-1}(z)` oriented right-to-left.

A Schur path starts at a nonbasis terminal in `C^partial` and ends at a free right vertex in `O`.

Two structural facts are immediate:

1. every internal `B` vertex is entered only through its unique matched edge from its partner in `Z`, so an internal matched pair `z,b` is traversed consecutively as one unit;
2. a deep nonbasis vertex in `C^circ` cannot occur on a directed Schur path at all, because no directed edge enters a nonbasis left vertex.

Because the Section 174 shield is basis-closed,

`b in W iff mu_0(b) in W`.

Thus a shielded matched pair can be contracted to one path-capacity vertex.

## 2. Contracted shield capacity

Put

`p_W := |B cap W| = |Z cap W|`,

`c_W := |C^partial cap W|`,

`o_W := |O cap W|`.

Define

`kappa(W):=p_W+c_W+o_W`.

### Theorem BP1 — contracted shield path bound

At most `kappa(W)` paths in any pairwise vertex-disjoint directed `C^partial-to-O` path family can meet `W`.

### Proof

Contract every matching edge `z->b` with `b in B`, `z=mu_0(b)`, to one directed-gammoid vertex. Contraction preserves vertex-disjoint alternating linkages: every internal visit to `z` is followed by the unique matched step to `b`, and every internal visit to `b` is preceded by that matched step.

In the contracted graph a Schur path can meet the basis-closed shield only through one of:

- a shielded terminal in `C^partial`, of which there are `c_W`;
- a shielded contracted `B-Z` pair, of which there are `p_W`;
- a shielded sink in `O`, of which there are `o_W`.

Vertices in `C^circ cap W` are absent from every Schur path. Pairwise vertex-disjointness allows at most one path per listed contracted shield vertex. Summing gives `kappa(W)`. QED.

## 3. Strengthened sector rank and nullity inequalities

Retain the Section 174 sector sets `C_i^partial,O_i` outside `W`. Sector locality is unchanged.

Delete from a maximum Schur path family the paths meeting `W`. Theorem BP1 removes at most `kappa(W)` paths. Every remaining path stays in one sector and uses a distinct sink there. Therefore

### Theorem BP2 — basis-contracted sector rank bound

`rank S <= p_W+c_W+o_W + sum_i min(|C_i^partial|,|O_i|)`.

Subtract from

`|C^partial|=c_W+sum_i |C_i^partial|`.

The shielded terminal count cancels exactly, giving

### Corollary BP3 — improved sector nullity

`zeta >= sum_i max(0, |C_i^partial|-|O_i|) - p_W-o_W`.

Compare this with Section 174.19:

`zeta >= sum_i max(0, |C_i^partial|-|O_i|) - |W\C^partial|`.

Since the full shield decomposes as

`W=(B cap W) sqcup (Z cap W) sqcup (C^circ cap W) sqcup (C^partial cap W) sqcup (O cap W)`,

basis closure gives

`|W\C^partial|=2p_W+|C^circ cap W|+o_W`.

Thus BP3 saves exactly

`p_W+|C^circ cap W|`

units over the promoted Section 174 bound.

## 4. New exact closing criterion

The locked sector branch now closes whenever

`sum_i max(0, |C_i^partial|-|O_i|) >= s+p_W+o_W`.

Using the local population identity (174.17), this is equivalently

`sum_i max(0, |X_i|-|Z_i|-|O_i|-|C_i^circ|) >= s+p_W+o_W`.

This strictly strengthens the previous sufficient theorem (174.23) whenever the shield contains a basis pair or a deep nonbasis vertex.

## 5. Dual negative-sector form

Use the notation of `target_a_sector_deficit_duality_2026-09-04.md`. Let

`J=rho^dagger-|Y_0|`,

`g=J-h=Delta_Lambda-d_sc`,

and let `O_iso` be the surviving exterior vertices with no surviving response neighbor. Put

`Q_Sigma=sum_i max(0, |O_i|-|C_i^partial|)`.

The exact signed sector sum is

`sum_i (|C_i^partial|-|O_i|)`

`=s-J-c_W+o_W+|O_iso|`.

Therefore the BP3 closing criterion is equivalent to

### Corollary BP4 — contracted deficit amplification

`Q_Sigma >= J+p_W+c_W-|O_iso|`.

Equivalently,

`Q_Sigma-p_W-c_W+|O_iso|-h >= g`.

The old Section 174 criterion had the larger shield correction `|W\O|-|O_iso|`. The new correction depends only on shielded basis pairs and shielded Schur terminals; shielded deep nonbasis vertices and the duplicate `Z` endpoint of each basis pair no longer cost rank.

## 6. Next target

The remaining shield cost is now matroid-sensitive:

`p_W=|B cap W|`.

The Schur nullity is basis-invariant, so one may choose the `Z`-basis and its perfect matching after the stress fan is fixed. A natural next theorem is to minimize `p_W` over all `Z`-perfect basis matchings, equivalently a minimum-crossing matching problem for the preliminary geometric shield.
